      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Key Service**\n\nI'm zeroing in on Google Cloud KMS for the managed key service. The next step is to solidify how to identify it within the `envelope_encrypt.py` code, ensuring a clear integration with the Google Cloud KMS client library. It feels like a solid foundation to move forward on.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Implementation**\n\nI've determined that `envelope_encrypt.py` will leverage Google Cloud KMS and its Python client library. I'm focusing on incorporating `google.cloud.kms_v1` and `base64` imports. The encryption process will involve a KMS client, key path definition, and the use of the `encrypt` method for a DEK encrypted by KMS, followed by the actual data encryption. I'll hardcode a key path placeholder, assuming key details are user-provided.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866387566,
          "start": 1789866381978
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc59929a001k8hbQfshbOdfIz",
